            This directory contains modified versions of the upstream files.

Removed from upstream: Demo/, Tests/, media/, .github/, .spi.yml, CONTRIBUTING.md,
the MarkdownEngineCodeBlocks and MarkdownEngineLatex targets (and their
HighlighterSwift / SwiftMath dependencies). Package.swift lists only MarkdownEngine.
The upstream test suite (532 tests) passed against the modified sources with all
new switches at their defaults. That run does not cover items 11 and later: some upstream
tests use APIs removed in item 12 (`SyntaxHighlighter.backgroundColor()`, the table
`codeBackgroundColor` parameters), and BottomOverscrollPolicyTests expects the old
overscroll default (item 16).

Changes by Marc (all marked with `// Marc:` or in files starting with a Marc comment):

1. NativeTextViewWrapper: new public hooks and init parameters
   - onTextViewReady: ((NSTextView) -> Void)?   (async on main queue after creation)
   - onWillPaste: ((NSTextView, NSPasteboard) -> Bool)?
   - onDropFiles: ((NSTextView, NSDraggingInfo, Int) -> Bool)?   (Int = UTF-16 insertion index)
   - onSaveRequest: ((NSTextView) -> Bool)?   (the `saveDocument:` action)
   - onDocumentShown: ((String) -> Void)?   (async on main queue, once per document after its
     text, scroll offset and selection are in)
2. NativeTextView+PasteHandling: paste(_:) calls onWillPaste first. pasteAsPlainText(_:)
   (⌥⇧⌘V) is overridden: it inserts the plain-text flavor and bypasses onWillPaste and the
   engine's HTML conversion. validateUserInterfaceItem accepts saveDocument:.
3. NativeTextView+FileDrop.swift (new): registers .fileURL drag type, calls onDropFiles
   from performDragOperation; false falls back to AppKit's default.
4. NativeTextView+SaveRequest.swift (new): `saveDocument:` responder that calls
   onSaveRequest, else forwards to the next responder (the NSDocument).
5. Services/FileImageProvider.swift (new): EmbeddedImageProvider that resolves
   `![x](relative/path.png)` against a base directory URL (also absolute paths, file: URLs,
   `<...>` destinations, titles, percent escapes). Set via configuration.services.images.
6. Configuration/MarkdownEngineFeatures.swift (new): global switches wikiLinks, imageEmbeds,
   latex, arrowSubstitution (defaults true = upstream behavior). disableNonGFM() turns all off.
   Used in InlineParser.matchBuiltIn, BlockParser.isBlockLatexOpen, WikiLinkService
   (display text == raw text when off), MarkdownListHandler (no `[[` completion, no `->` arrow).
7. Extensions (==highlight==) and directives (@name) are already off by default upstream
   (empty `configuration.extensions` / `.directives`); Marc registers only StrikethroughExtension.
8. Key bindings: the engine binds none of the shortcuts Marc uses (checked: it has no
   key-equivalent or menu code besides ⌘↵ for wiki previews, which is inert with wiki links off).
   Nothing had to be removed.
9. NativeTextViewWrapper.updateNSView: configuration.paragraph (line height extra spacing,
   paragraph spacing) is synced at runtime and triggers a rebuild like a font change.
   Upstream only applied it in makeNSView.
10. NativeTextView+FrameAndOverscroll: scrollRangeToVisible uses the engine's explicit reveal in
   full-width mode too (upstream: reading column only). Native NSTextView reveal does not scroll
   through the NativeTextViewContainer document view, so arrow keys did not scroll the document.
11. MarkdownEditorTheme: new colors codeBlockBackground, codeBlockLanguage, inlineCodeBackground,
   inlineCodeText, blockquoteBar, blockquoteBackground, blockquoteText, tableBorder,
   tableHeaderBackground, tableStripeBackground, and the helper NSColor.overlay(dark:light:).
   Upstream took the code fill from the syntax highlighter and drew quote bars, quote text and
   table lines in mutedText.
12. Code blocks are marked with a new `.codeBlockBackground` attribute (theme color), and
   MarkdownTextLayoutFragment finds them by that attribute. Upstream compared `.backgroundColor`
   with SyntaxHighlighter.backgroundColor(); that protocol method, the styler's codeBackground /
   codeBackgroundColor fields and the table codeBackgroundColor parameters are removed.
   Also new: CodeBlockStyle.backgroundOutset (default 0) lets the fill reach past the text
   column; fill edges round to the pixel instead of floor/ceil (no seam with translucent fills);
   while the opening fence is hidden, its language is drawn in the block's top-right corner
   (`.codeBlockLanguage` attribute).
13. Inline code: a rounded pill drawn by the fragment (`.inlineCodeBackground` attribute) instead
   of a `.backgroundColor` glyph-box fill; hidden backticks get a kern so the pill has padding.
   Table cells keep a glyph-box fill (theme.inlineCodeBackground) because they are rasterized.
14. Block quotes: MarkdownASTStyler.styleBlockquote collects lines first and tags each line with
   `.blockquoteEdges` (where each level's panel opens and closes). The fragment draws an
   optional rounded panel (theme.blockquoteBackground, BlockquoteStyle.panelPadding) with the
   bar at its left edge; this replaces drawBlockquoteBars. blockquoteIndentPerLevel is 20
   (upstream 18); text indent is level × indent (upstream plus half a level).
15. Tables: drawn as a card with a rounded outline, header fill and striped body rows (theme
   colors). Upstream drew a square border with column and row separators. The table image cache
   key includes the new colors.
16. OverscrollPolicy.percent default is 0.25 (upstream 0.5).
17. Raw source mode: light highlighting (Styling/SourceHighlighter.swift, new) on rebuild and,
   after each edit, for the edited lines, their neighbors and touching code blocks
   (NativeTextViewCoordinator.highlightRawSource). Base attributes come from a memoized
   makeBaseAttributes. BlockLevelTokenizer.isTableSeparator and incrementalBacktickCensus are
   internal (upstream private) for this.
18. Per-document text binding: the coordinator takes the wrapper's current binding on every
   updateNSView (setTextBinding), and edits go through scheduleTextPush to the binding of the
   document that made them, also when the embedder switched documents before the push. The
   outgoing undo snapshot comes from the synchronous storage, not lastSyncedText. The selection
   of each document is saved on switch-away, restored (clamped) on switch-back, and pruned with
   the undo stacks. With wiki links off, a raw mode toggle keeps the undo stack.
